& [Step01_Authority] is fail closed
  + verify raw source, source manifest, processing input manifest, audit, every SJS stage hash, predecessor canonical hashes and signatures, phase lock, and both replacement signatures
  + verify both signatures name the same canonical revision but retain separate module scopes and supersession edges
  + stop before code on any drift, omission, contradiction, or partial signature

& [Step02_PreimplementationBaseline] is measured
  + record hashes for phase3_evidence.rs, topology_forms.rs, Cargo.toml, and Cargo.lock
  + run focused existing machine-form and topology-form tests before modification
  + confirm current legacy symbols occur only on the expected production and governed support surfaces

& [Step03_Phase3MachineForms] is exact
  + change PHASE3_MACHINE_FORMS_PROFILE from 0.1 to 0.2
  + replace ConsistencyClass with public InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + replace QuiescentDoubleInventory with NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + retain OsSnapshotProven
  + retain exact snake_case serde and pure ValidatePhase3 for the closed two-variant enum
  + add rustdoc that structural validity is not acquisition or issuer proof
  + change no unrelated form, validator, field, constant, or public behavior

& [Step04_TopologyForms] is exact
  + change TOPOLOGY_FORMS_PROFILE from 0.2 to 0.3
  + change TOPOLOGY_RECEIPT_PROFILE from 0.2 to 0.3
  + leave WINDOWS_TOPOLOGY_PROFILE exactly 0.1
  + import InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + replace TopologyReceipt.consistency with required consistency_evidence in the same semantic position
  + permit only NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual in receipt 0.3
  + reject OsSnapshotProven with Receipt at consistency_evidence and exact bounded message
  + add rustdoc denying acquisition, issuance, and state proof
  + preserve every unrelated receipt invariant and validation order

& [Step05_CompileMigration] is strict
  + revise every in-repository current Rust caller and fixture to the new type, variant, and field explicitly
  + add no alias, default, conversion, parser, rewrite, or compatibility module
  + let unknown external compile callers fail rather than silently reinterpret meaning

& [Step06_LegacyFixtures] is direct
  + prove old enum token rejection
  + prove old receipt profile rejection in otherwise current-shaped data
  + prove old consistency field rejection
  + prove missing consistency_evidence rejection
  + prove simultaneous old and new fields rejection
  + prove old token in the new field rejects
  + prove OsSnapshotProven returns exact Receipt fault at consistency_evidence

& [Step07_PositiveAndInvariantTests] is complete
  + prove exact three revised profiles and unchanged scanner profile
  + prove exact snake_case serialization for both enum variants
  + prove current valid receipt round-trip with non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal
  + rerun every preexisting receipt invariant and negative case
  + prove enum structural validation accepts both variants while receipt semantic validation admits only the weaker current grade

& [Step08_StaticBoundary] is independent
  + require InventoryConsistencyEvidence, NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual, consistency_evidence, and new profiles
  + reject ConsistencyClass, QuiescentDoubleInventory, quiescent_double_inventory, legacy field declarations, aliases, defaults, conversions, extra variants, direct reconciliation-to-receipt conversion, producer or consumer APIs, unsafe, platform, filesystem, clock, and effect surfaces
  + assert exactly two production modules changed and no Cargo or lockfile delta
  + scan documentation for explicit evidence-versus-proof nonclaims

& [Step09_FocusedVerification] is proportional
  + run machine-forms and topology-forms unit, static, and evidence tests in debug
  + run the same focused set in unique-metadata overflow-checked release
  + perform no physical fixture or effect-bearing builder invocation

& [Step10_GlobalVerification] is complete
  + run complete workspace tests in debug and unique-metadata overflow-checked release while retaining the governed physical ignore
  + run format check, warnings-denied workspace lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, and dependency audit
  + confirm test counts and exact expected ignore count

& [Step11_EvidenceMigration] is governed
  + update phase3 machine-forms evidence builder, manifest, and evidence assertion to the machine-forms replacement signature and joint canonical revision
  + update topology-forms evidence builder, manifest, and evidence assertion to the topology-forms replacement signature and joint canonical revision
  + update current dependent topology evidence builders and assertions from the superseded topology signature to its replacement
  + preserve frozen historical manifests and proof bytes unchanged
  + add one subject-local revision evidence manifest and proof surface if required by the final evidence design

& [Step12_Closure] is recursive
  + create solution, completion review, proof, turn, file-change, narrative, reentry, registry, requirement, slice, readiness, and plan updates
  + rehash current evidence manifests dependency-first and verify zero stale records
  + verify source, SJS, canonical, phase lock, signature, module, evidence, and proof hashes
  + reapply C01 through C24 after all closure artifacts

& [Step13_Publication] is pure milestone release
  + review exact production and support diffs against the signed slice
  + commit and push implementation separately from proof closure when useful for exact implementation identity
  + leave a clean tree and precise reentry

& [Rollback] is exact
  + restore only phase3_evidence.rs, topology_forms.rs, their current tests and evidence support, and revision closure artifacts to the pre-revision commit
  + restore current evidence references to the two predecessor signatures if implementation is rolled back
  + retain raw source, SJS artifacts, supersession history, and proof records
  + no database migration, physical cleanup, receipt invalidation, or external coordination exists

& [Stop] is mandatory
  + stop on source or predecessor drift, missing signature, old-schema acceptance, snapshot receipt success, supplied-pair acquisition claim, scanner profile change, unrelated receipt delta, third production module, alias, migration, default, conversion, dependency, unsafe, platform call, filesystem, clock, producer, consumer, effect, stale evidence, or failed proof
  + all physical tests and effect-bearing builders remain uninvoked
